> I don't think my attempt to generalize this to the case of multiple predictors was successful. My guess is that this is because the predictors are correlated.

Correct!  The explained variance with 2 correlated predictors must also account for (twice) the covariance:

num := (g1^2)*0.2503654 + (g2^2)*0.2352602 + 2*g1*0.06019934*g2

